## External integration docs (optional)

Cache vendor APIs/XSDs/PDFs/OpenAPI under `.work/docs/integration/`. Rules: organize by source+version subfolders; log downloads in `.work/docs/integration/MANIFEST.txt`; prefer official domains; never store keys/PEM/tokens/`.env`; verify file type after download; vendor artifacts only. Read cached copies during implementation.

---

## Protected Files

- **File access override:** read any path the user provides, regardless of `.gitignore`.
- **Do NOT modify unless explicitly asked:** `.work/PROTECTED_SURFACES.json` plus `package.json`, `docker-compose*.yml`, `Dockerfile.*`, `frontend/vite.config.ts`, `frontend/tsconfig.json`, `frontend/package.json`, `.env*` (except `.env.example`).
- **If a protected file needs a change:** stop, explain why, ask permission.

---

## Data Privacy & Security

- **Sensitive data:** keep production/customer data local without approval; use repo sanitizer (e.g. `.obfuscation/sanitize_data.py`) before loading exports; prefer sanitized copies.
- **No PII in logs:** log internal IDs/status only; sanitize errors.
- **Debug scripts:** no embedded sensitive data; use `.env` or runtime values; ask before re-running when a var is missing.
- **Secret scrubbing:** redact keys/tokens/passwords as `[REDACTED]`; never display credentials or raw `.env`.
- **Test data:** synthetic/mock only; never hardcode real emails/IDs; no unsanitized prod dumps in tests. Ad-hoc DB mutations need explicit in-message approval; prefer fixtures/mocks.
- **File hygiene:** delete temp files; write exports to `tmp/`, not the source tree.

---

## Database & Schema Rules (v1 — Redis only)

- **Storage:** no SQL database in v1; Redis ephemeral keys only (pairing relay, TTL).
- **If SQL is added later:** idempotent scripts under `migrations/` via `@db-migration`; models are source of truth; permanent append-only schema ledger; never prune.
- **Startup verify:** after `bin/start.sh` or `docker compose up`, confirm `GET /health` and Redis reachable.
- **Exceptions:** one-off/destructive/manual migrations and ad-hoc `INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE` on shared DBs require explicit human approval in-message — present exact SQL; the human runs it.
- **Backfills: STRICTLY PROHIBITED** by agents against shared DBs — describe SQL for manual execution.

---

## Docker / Dev Environment

When the project uses Compose, **never** run bare `npm/yarn/python/pytest` or type-checkers on the host — run all test/lint/type commands inside the documented compose service.

| Service | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `api` | FastAPI pairing API + health |
| `frontend` | Vite dev server / static SPA |
| `redis` | Ephemeral pairing relay (TTL) |
| `caddy` | Reverse proxy |

Stack identity: `.env` (`COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME`, host ports). Prefer **`bin/start.sh`**.

```bash
# API
docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.yml exec api sh -c "cd /app && pytest tests/ -q"
docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.yml exec api sh -c "cd /app && ruff check ."
docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.yml exec api sh -c "cd /app && pyright ."
# Frontend
docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.yml exec frontend sh -c "cd /app && npm run lint"
docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.yml exec frontend sh -c "cd /app && npm run typecheck"
docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.yml exec frontend sh -c "cd /app && npm test"
# One-off script
docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.yml exec api sh -c "cd /app && timeout 120 python scripts/my_script.py"
```

Skills (`code-implementation`, `code-verify`) must use these commands — not hardcoded names from another project. Place one-off scripts under **`bin/`**.

---

## Workflow Rules

- **Planning:** plans live under `.work/plans/`. Wait for approval before large code changes when a plan-only was requested; confirm before editing when scope is unclear.
- **Deletion:** NEVER delete files without explicit user permission.
- **Git:**
  - NEVER `git commit`/`push` unless the user requests it in the same message.
  - `@session-control close commit` / `commit push`: MUST run `git add` + `git commit` per `.ai/skills/session-control/skill.md` (C4b) — stage all safe dirty paths (default scope), then `git push` if requested. Show `git log -1 --oneline` + `git status -sb`; no "committed" claim without a SHA.
  - Never modify history (rebase, force-push) without explicit request.
  - `prepare-commit-msg` hook auto-prepends task refs when the branch contains one; don't bypass hooks unless the user requests `--no-verify`.
- **No attribution:** never add "Generated by", "Created by", dates, or agent signatures.
- **No `Co-authored-by:`:** never add co-author trailers or `--trailer`. Hooks installed via `@deploy-basic update` (or `bash /mnt/work/Projects/.ai/scripts/install-git-hooks.sh`).

---

## Verification & Communication

- **Before "complete":** run applicable tests + lint/type; confirm no regression; report actual output, not assumed.
- **On failure:** report exact error, diagnose root cause, fix, re-run.
- **Scope:** declare scope first (§ Change safety); touch-scope + blast-radius enforce it.
- **Communication:** be concise; surface blockers early; label uncertainty; distinguish confirmed facts / inferences / proposals.

---

## External docs

Use Context7 MCP (`@upstash/context7-mcp`) for version-specific library docs when configured; else web-search to verify current APIs before writing integration code.

---

## Commit Message Format

- Plain text; no surrounding quotes or wrapping parentheses.
- Subject (≤72 chars, imperative): `REF-123: subject` when a ref is known, else `type: description`.
- Types (no ref): `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `docs`, `chore`, `style`, `test`.
- Correct: `fix: handle empty payload on webhook retry` · Wrong: `"fix(webhook): empty payload"`.

---

## Documentation layout (`.ai/` vs `.work/`)

- **`.ai/`:** framework-only (skills, concepts, guides, templates). Thin-client: resolves from `$AGENT_OS_SOURCE`; never created by `@deploy-basic`.
- **`.work/`:** all project-specific memory — plans, SPECs, ADRs, `HANDOFF.md`, `PROTECTED_SURFACES.json`, binding `.work/standards/`, `.work/docs/`. Always local.

| Path | Layer |
|------|-------|
| `.work/plans/` | Plans, registries, `NEXT.md` |
| `.work/features/` | Feature SPECs |
| `.work/decisions/` | ADRs |
| `.work/context/HANDOFF.md` | Session handoff |
| `.work/standards/` | Binding engineering standards |
| `.work/docs/integration/` | Vendor/API integration cache |
| `.ai/skills/` | Portable agent skills |

Canonical map: `.ai/README.md` · Working tree: `.work/README.md`.

